            "eyebrow": "Meet our founder",
            "heading": "Pastor Joseph Cotton Jr.",
            "body": "<p><strong>The Heart Behind Our Mission</strong></p><p>Pastor Joseph Cotton Jr. was born in Oakland, California, and has been a faithful member of Acts Full Gospel Church since 2003. He currently serves as the Assistant Pastor of Acts Full Gospel Church in Oakland, California, where he has dedicated his life to ministry, leadership, mentoring, and community outreach.</p><p>On May 1, 2018, Pastor Cotton was appointed Executive Director of the Men of Valor Academy, where he continues his passion for developing men of integrity, character, and faith.</p><p>Pastor Cotton served as the Head Chaplain at Juvenile Hall for ten years, ministering to youth who were incarcerated for offenses including murder, robbery, rape, prostitution, and other serious crimes. Through his leadership, mentorship, and commitment to rehabilitation, he played an instrumental role in helping reduce the Juvenile Hall population from approximately 370 youth to just 68.</p>",
